<title>UK: P&amp;U to take 10 to 16 cents/shr charge.</title>
<headline>P&amp;U to take 10 to 16 cents/shr charge.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn Inc said on Tuesday it would take a one-off charge of between $0.10 and $0.16 per share after tax against third-quarter earnings, to cover costs related to the planned merger of Pharmacia Biotech with Amersham International Plc's Life Science business.  </p>
<p>The company said it expected to incur a number of charges including the write-off of some acquired research and development costs linked to the creation of Amersham Pharmacia Biotech, in which it will have a 45 percent stake.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
